  scene.wrong: { type: int, default: 0 }
---

## Valves

@narrator: The key turns on the bottom of the black tub. The valves are stiff with forty years of lime.
@nell{mono when="entry.drawing.read"}: Blue first, then red, then let it go. A child drew that. A child who had watched.
<branch id="first" prompt="Which valve first?">
  <choice id="blue" label="The blue valve">
    @narrator: Cold water coughs into the tub. The surface trembles; the key rolls over once.
  </choice>
  <choice id="red" label="The red valve">
    @narrator: The pipe screams. Steam comes off the black water and the canvas lid of the next tub flaps like something is breathing under it.
    ::set{scene.wrong += 1}
  </choice>
</branch>
<branch id="second" prompt="Then?">
  <choice id="red" label="The red valve">
    @narrator: Hot meets cold. The black water begins, very slowly, to turn clear.
  </choice>
  <choice id="blue" label="More cold">
    @narrator: The water rises over the lip of the tub and across the tiles, towards the drain in the floor, which is plugged with hair.
    ::set{scene.wrong += 1}
  </choice>
</branch>
::next{to="flooded" when="scene.wrong >= 2"}
<branch id="third" prompt="And then?">
  <choice id="drain" label="Pull the chain">
    @narrator: A gulp from deep in the building, and the tub empties in one long swallow.
  </choice>
  <choice id="wait" label="Wait and watch">
    @narrator: You wait. The water waits with you. Then the canvas lid of the next tub lifts, a finger's width.
    ::set{scene.wrong += 1}
  </choice>
</branch>
::next{to="flooded" when="scene.wrong >= 2"}
<match on="scene.wrong">
  <when is="0">
    @narrator: The brass key lies in the empty tub in a ring of grey silt. It is warm, like it's been held.
    ::give{item="brassKey"}
    ::assert{solved(hydroValves)}
  </when>
  <otherwise>
    @narrator: The water rises to your waist before you get the door open and fall out onto the corridor floor. The key is still down there.
    ::fright{amount=2}
  </otherwise>
</match>
::end{reason="valves"}
::mark{id="flooded"}
@narrator: The door behind you is shut. You do not remember it shutting. The water is at your chest, then your chin, and the canvas lids are all open now.
@maud{vo}: In you go, dear. It's only water. It's only the night.
::set{run.fate = "drowned"}
::set{user.deaths += 1}
::end{reason="drowned"}
